2125. Number of Laser Beams in a Bank
Leetcode Link: https://leetcode.com/problems/number-of-laser-beams-in-a-bank/description/


Intuition (5–6 lines)

1️ A laser beam exists only between two rows that both have devices.
2️ Also, there must be no devices in between rows → so only consecutive non-empty rows matter.
3️ Count number of '1's (devices) in each row.
4️ For two valid rows with counts a and b, beams = a × b (each device connects to all in next row).
5️ Skip rows with 0 devices (they break the connection chain).
6️ Keep track of previous non-empty row (prev) and multiply with current (c).

 Why prev * c?
If:

Row1 → 3 devices  
Row2 → 2 devices  

Beams:

3 × 2 = 6

Every device in Row1 connects to every device in Row2.

Time Complexity (TC)
O(m × n)
Space Complexity (SC)
O(1)

class Solution {
    public int numberOfBeams(String[] bank) {
        int n=bank.length;
        int ans=0;
        int prev=0;
        for(int i=0;i<bank[0].length();i++){
            if(bank[0].charAt(i)=='1')prev++;
        }

        for(int i=1;i<n;i++){
            int c=0;
            for(int j=0;j<bank[i].length();j++){
                if(bank[i].charAt(j)=='1')c++;
            }
            if(c!=0){
            ans+=(prev*c);
            prev=c;
            }
        }
        return ans;
    }
}
